<?php $title='John Little | Midcity Handyman & Remodeling';$description='Meet John Little, founder of Midcity Handyman & Remodeling and the owner responsible for scope, project communication, and client accountability.';include __DIR__.'/../includes/header.php';?><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Meet the owner</p><h1>John Little</h1><p class="lead">Founder of Midcity Handyman & Remodeling, serving Western New York homeowners with clear communication, written scopes, and finished work done right.</p></div></section><section class="section white"><div class="wrap split"><img loading="lazy" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1560250097-0b93528c311a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=82" alt="Owner of a remodeling company"><div><p class="eyebrow">Why John started Mid City</p><h2>The problem was not a shortage of contractors. It was a shortage of accountability.</h2><p>John kept seeing homeowners struggle to find a contractor who showed up, communicated clearly, and finished the agreed work. Mid City focuses on the projects Western New York homeowners and property operators need most, managed through one repeatable process.</p><p>Every project starts with an on-site visit. John walks the space, asks the right questions, explains realistic options, and turns the discussion into a written scope. When conditions or decisions change, clients hear about it before the change affects budget or timeline.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Book a Site Visit</a></div></div></section><?php include __DIR__.'/../includes/footer.php';?>
